# TypeScript module patterns

## File naming

- `*.adapter.ts` — pluggable implementations (auth, storage)
- `*.plugin.ts` — Fastify plugins only
- `*.types.ts` — interfaces and domain types, no runtime logic
- `room-store.ts`, `*-service.ts` — business logic

## Imports

- Domain modules (`rooms/`, `auth/`) must not import from `routes/` or `plugins/`
- Use explicit types; avoid `any`
- ESM: use `.js` extension in relative imports when targeting `dist/` (NodeNext)

## Fastify

- Register routes via async plugins, not inline in `index.ts` (after step 0.4)
- Use `fastify-plugin` when a plugin must share decorators (auth)

## Example adapter shape

```typescript
export interface AuthAdapter {
  authenticate(credentials: AuthCredentials): Promise<AuthUser>;
}
```

Swap implementation in bootstrap — never branch JWT vs session inside a route.
